“Go over to Daddy and show him how much you love him,” she had said to Felix earlier His clear understanding of what she meant showed how smart of a child he was.
Matthias paused for a moment, then, smiling, reciprocated his son’s kiss.
Delighted to have his love display returned, Felix burst into ecstatic laughter “Our next child is going to love you just as much as Felix,” Layla declared,
looking straight into Matthias’s eyes. “I know she will. I’m certain of it.”







The duke’s family left Arvis just as the cool wind that heralded the end of summer was starting to blow. They had only spent one season at Arvis, but Felix had grown a remarkable amount in that time, and the servants who had stayed behind at the Ratse mansion were amazed to see how much bigger he was.
Layla had spent the bulk of her time at Arvis studying in preparation for the upcoming semester, and learning to swim. Her academic achievements during the break were impressive; her swimming achievements, less so. Even after all her practice, she was by no means a good swimmer. However, she had gotten to the point where she could float in the water without screaming, and she felt proud of this modest accomplishment.
