Layla thought for a moment, then shook her head as she passed Felix back to the nanny and stood up. “No, I’d prefer to see him this evening, once I’m back from class.”
“Class? Goodness. Are you really still planning to go to class, Your Grace?” the nanny asked, sounding anxious.
Layla calmly nodded. “Yes I am. I’ll be back this afternoon,” she said, gently but firmly.
Knowing how stubborn the duchess could be, the nanny made no further attempt to dissuade her. Glancing outside, she caught a glimpse of the duchess’s shiny chrome bicycle next to one of the mansion’s flowerbeds. Turning back towards the duchess, she worriedly asked, “You’re not planning to ride your bicycle to campus, are you?”
Layla laughed and shook her head. “No, I’m not going to ride my bike.” “Good. Then I’ll summon the chauffeur right away—”
“I’m going to walk. I’ll just think of it as a pleasant strollSmiling brightly, she picked up her leather bag and slung it over her shoulder. The bag, which was the last birthday present Uncle Bill gave her, was quite worn out by now, but she intended to keep using il until she graduated from college.

The nanny and the maids continued to express concern, following her all the way out the mansion’s front door, but they were unable to talk the stubborn duchess out of her decision to walk to campus. After repeatedly assuring them that she would be fine, she started off towards campus with light steps, before suddenly stopping and turning to face them again. “Oh! After I see Dr. Pelles, I’m going to talk to the duke myself!”
The dazed looks on the maids’ faces quickly gave way to smiles just as bright as Layla’s.
“Yes, Your Grace!” they replied in unison. Their voices sounded like a chorus amid the autumn sunlight. “Don’t worry, we’ll keep your secret!”




