“Goodness, Matthias, goodness dear!” Elise repeated. It was all she could

say.








The VIP suite was divided into two rooms: the waiting room for guests, and the patient’s room, which in this case had also served as the birthing room.
Matthias slowly walked down the hallway between the two rooms. Each step he took rekindled memories of the baby’s conception, development, and birth.
He now knew what Layla’s belly looked like at full term, as well as what she thought and how much she smiled.
She had worried that he might find her ugly with such a big belly, but her worries were unfounded. Throughout her pregnancy, he found her dazzlingly beautiful.
